1104
00:48:46,940 --> 00:48:48,780
 Personal data.

1105
00:48:48,780 --> 00:48:56,800
 Everything from the GDPR stuff we talked about earlier still applies here.

1106
00:48:56,800 --> 00:49:00,190
 Two things are extra important in MongoDB.

1107
00:49:00,190 --> 00:49:05,680
 First, a flexible schema makes it tempting to save one more field.

1108
00:49:05,680 --> 00:49:08,520
 Like a birth date, for example.

1109
00:49:08,520 --> 00:49:10,300
 Don't unless you need it.

1110
00:49:11,060 --> 00:49:12,790
 Second, copies.

1111
00:49:12,790 --> 00:49:16,130
 If you copy the customer's name into every order,

1112
00:49:16,130 --> 00:49:24,730
 a request to be deleted, meaning finding and changing every copy.

1113
00:49:24,730 --> 00:49:30,870
 So for personal data, prefer references like I showed you earlier.

1114
00:49:30,870 --> 00:49:36,900
 So basically, collect only what you need.

1115
00:49:37,690 --> 00:49:39,070
 Keep it correct.

1116
00:49:39,070 --> 00:49:42,870
 Delete it when you no longer need it.

1117
00:49:42,870 --> 00:49:44,080
 And protect it.

1118
00:49:44,080 --> 00:49:50,670
 MongoDB makes two things easier to get wrong.

1119
00:49:50,670 --> 00:49:52,190
 First, the flexible schema.

1120
00:49:52,840 --> 00:49:57,140
 Adding a new field takes one line of code.

1121
00:49:57,140 --> 00:50:01,570
 So it's tempting to save things just in case.

1122
00:50:01,570 --> 00:50:03,770
 Like birthday, gender, location.

1123
00:50:03,770 --> 00:50:12,570
 Every extra field is personal data you are responsible for.

1124
00:50:12,570 --> 00:50:14,680
 Second, copies.

1125
00:50:14,680 --> 00:50:18,360
 If we copy a customer's name and address into every order,

1126
00:50:19,040 --> 00:50:25,890
 a request to be deleted means finding and changing every copy in every collection.

1127
00:50:25,890 --> 00:50:32,000
 So if you keep personal data in one place and reference it,

1128
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:40,670
 deleting or maybe anonymizing one customer is one update.

1129
00:50:40,670 --> 00:50:44,560
 So for personal data, prefer references, okay?

1130
00:50:45,280 --> 00:50:51,300
 And copy only what the law or the receipt requires.

